infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Two ways to isolate: thread pool vs semaphore
  desc Both cap concurrency per dependency — only a separate thread can abandon a hung call
  compares
    - label Thread-pool isolation
      children
        - label Runs on a separate pool thread
          desc Caller hands off the work and waits with its own timeout
        - label Abandons a hung call
          desc Caller's timeout frees it even though the pool thread stays stuck
        - label Pays a hand-off per call
          desc Hystrix default coreSize 10 — use for network calls that can hang
    - label Semaphore isolation
      children
        - label Runs on the caller's own thread
          desc Just a concurrency counter, near-zero overhead
        - label Can't unstick a hang
          desc A blocking call pins the caller; only new calls are stopped
        - label Near-zero overhead
          desc resilience4j maxConcurrentCalls 25 — use for fast non-blocking calls
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6
